      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 88. Pages: NC State, MBG (two Plant Finder pages cached; the second is the cultivar 'Little Lucky Peach Glow' and not cited) and ASPCA. RHS not read (hand-fetch budget kept for calamondin and tulip; RHS pages are not in the cache), so hardiness is left empty: MBG gives top growth hardy in USDA 10 to 11 and roots to zone 9, NC State 7a to 11b, and the RHS H-scale needs a UK source. Lifecycle perennial is the agent's choice: NC State lists annual and perennial, MBG says gardeners in cold climates treat it as an annual. The Spanish shop plant of row 88 is often Lantana montevidensis (trailing lantana, lantana rastrera), a different species; lantana is invasive in warm regions (MBG, NC State: weedy). Toxicity: ASPCA toxic to dogs, cats and horses (triterpenoids, liver failure more common in livestock); NC State medium severity for people (lantadenes), leaves and unripe berries minor skin irritation, contact dermatitis yes. Grades of 2 are the agent's mapping of toxic plus medium. Watering style a mapping, 5 days a guess. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
